1
00:00:00,084 --> 00:00:02,044
Grew up in the military,
worked in the military.

2
00:00:02,128 --> 00:00:03,796
Always told where to go, when to be there.

3
00:00:03,879 --> 00:00:05,423
I wanted to see my country
on my own terms.

4
00:00:05,506 --> 00:00:08,426
Motels, cash, fake names, travel light.

5
00:00:08,509 --> 00:00:11,178
Mostly, I take buses or hitchhike.
You get used to it.

6
00:00:11,262 --> 00:00:14,056
Command at
the 110th Special Investigations Unit

7
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:15,474
of the Military Police.

8
00:00:15,558 --> 00:00:17,393
It's not just 'cause
you need to put things right.

9
00:00:17,476 --> 00:00:18,978
And it's not because
you love the little guy.

10
00:00:19,061 --> 00:00:20,354
It's 'cause you hate the big guy.

11
00:00:20,438 --> 00:00:22,481
You hate the smug sons of bitches

12
00:00:22,565 --> 00:00:24,275
who think they can just
get away with things.

13
00:00:24,358 --> 00:00:25,860
You just figured that out?

14
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:38,164
Hundred thousand years ago,

15
00:00:38,247 --> 00:00:39,999
there were people who stayed
by the campfire,

16
00:00:40,082 --> 00:00:41,625
and people who wandered.

17
00:00:42,918 --> 00:00:46,464
I'm pretty sure I'm a direct descendant
of the wandering type.

18
00:00:46,547 --> 00:00:48,340
It's just who I am.

19
00:01:15,868 --> 00:01:16,994
♪ Chicken stuff ♪

20
00:01:38,766 --> 00:01:40,309
Whiz wit.

21
00:01:59,495 --> 00:02:01,413
Northbound train
now boarding.

22
00:02:01,497 --> 00:02:03,582
Service continues to Ellsworth-Federal,

23
00:02:03,666 --> 00:02:06,460
Spring Garden, City Hall and beyond.

24
00:03:36,383 --> 00:03:38,344
I need to see your hands.

25
00:03:42,431 --> 00:03:44,141
May I sit next to you?

26
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:46,393
Leave me alone.

27
00:03:46,477 --> 00:03:48,145
I can't do that.

28
00:03:50,814 --> 00:03:52,149
Go away.

29
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:54,193
There's only a few people on the train.

30
00:03:56,195 --> 00:03:58,864
If you waited till rush hour,
your plan would be more effective.

31
00:04:02,076 --> 00:04:04,870
Just... one hand.

32
00:04:07,289 --> 00:04:08,457
Just take out one hand.

33
00:04:09,917 --> 00:04:11,168
I can't.

34
00:04:11,251 --> 00:04:12,711
Yes, you can.

35
00:04:12,795 --> 00:04:14,964
What you have in there is very dangerous.

36
00:04:15,047 --> 00:04:17,216
The less contact
you have with it, the better.

37
00:04:18,342 --> 00:04:19,593
Easy.

38
00:04:20,844 --> 00:04:22,805
Don't do anything you can't undo.

39
00:04:24,682 --> 00:04:26,183
Show me one hand.

40
00:04:28,852 --> 00:04:29,895
Please.

41
00:04:40,489 --> 00:04:42,241
Thank you.

42
00:04:46,453 --> 00:04:47,997
Now...

43
00:04:49,873 --> 00:04:51,000
...show me what you have.

44
00:04:52,459 --> 00:04:53,544
I need to see it.

45
00:04:53,627 --> 00:04:54,878
Please.

46
00:04:56,839 --> 00:04:58,924
Go away.

47
00:04:59,008 --> 00:05:00,300
I can't do that.

48
00:05:00,384 --> 00:05:02,720
-Why?
-Because I'm involved now.

49
00:05:02,803 --> 00:05:04,638
Whatever you're in, I'm in it now, too.

50
00:05:06,598 --> 00:05:07,641
Just...

51
00:05:07,725 --> 00:05:10,227
take it out of the bag.

52
00:05:16,191 --> 00:05:18,027
That's better than
the bomb I thought you had.

53
00:05:19,528 --> 00:05:21,238
You don't have a problem with me.

54
00:05:21,321 --> 00:05:22,781
You don't even know me.

55
00:05:25,492 --> 00:05:27,703
It's over.

56
00:05:27,786 --> 00:05:29,288
It's all over.

57
00:05:29,913 --> 00:05:31,040
What is?

58
00:05:32,708 --> 00:05:33,834
Just talk to me.

59
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:38,172
I can help you.

60
00:05:39,923 --> 00:05:41,717
I'm a cop.

61
00:05:47,097 --> 00:05:48,515
You're a cop?

62
00:05:52,686 --> 00:05:54,563
No one can help me now.

63
00:05:54,646 --> 00:05:56,815
Oh, shit, man!

64
00:06:37,189 --> 00:06:39,566
Mr. Reacher, Detective Shaun Docherty.

65
00:06:39,650 --> 00:06:41,860
This is my partner Detective Tamara Green.

66
00:06:41,944 --> 00:06:44,029
We have a few questions for you.

67
00:06:44,113 --> 00:06:47,241
Shouldn't take too long if you're honest
and cooperative.

68
00:06:47,324 --> 00:06:48,700
Easy enough, right?

69
00:06:53,372 --> 00:06:55,666
Right? So...

70
00:06:55,749 --> 00:06:57,167
Okay, you, uh,

71
00:06:57,251 --> 00:07:00,087
you had a passport on you,
but no driver's license.

72
00:07:02,881 --> 00:07:03,882
No answer for that?

73
00:07:03,966 --> 00:07:05,425
It wasn't a question.

74
00:07:08,303 --> 00:07:09,680
Where do you currently live?

75
00:07:09,763 --> 00:07:11,265
What's the address of this building?

76
00:07:11,348 --> 00:07:13,475
-Why?
-It's where I'm currently living.

77
00:07:13,559 --> 00:07:14,852
Where's your home, asshole?

78
00:07:14,935 --> 00:07:15,853
Don't have one.

79
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:17,187
So you're homeless.

80
00:07:17,271 --> 00:07:18,939
Now I see why you're a detective.

81
00:07:19,022 --> 00:07:20,649
Motherfucker!

82
00:07:20,732 --> 00:07:23,318
You think I haven't
dealt with wiseasses before?

83
00:07:23,402 --> 00:07:26,321
Okay, okay. Let's try this.

84
00:07:26,405 --> 00:07:28,115
Where were you before the subway, Reacher?

85
00:07:28,198 --> 00:07:29,533
The Uptown on Frankfort.

86
00:07:29,616 --> 00:07:30,534
Listening to music.

87
00:07:30,617 --> 00:07:32,077
Then you went straight to the subway.

88
00:07:32,161 --> 00:07:34,079
No. Then, I got a cheesesteak.

89
00:07:34,163 --> 00:07:35,539
You ate a cheesesteak at 2:00 a.m.?

90
00:07:35,622 --> 00:07:37,624
-I'm in Philly.
-Why?

91
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:39,459
'Cause they taste good.

92
00:07:39,543 --> 00:07:41,545
Why-- Jesus tap-dancing Christ.

93
00:07:41,628 --> 00:07:43,755
Why are you in Philadelphia?
'Cause you don't sound like

94
00:07:43,839 --> 00:07:45,340
-you're from here.
-Phillies have a kid

95
00:07:45,424 --> 00:07:47,301
who consistently throws over 100.

96
00:07:47,384 --> 00:07:49,344
Wanted to see him play
before he blows his arm out.

97
00:07:49,428 --> 00:07:51,638
Oh, but instead,
you blow a woman's brains out.

98
00:07:51,722 --> 00:07:54,600
I didn't kill her. I don't even know her.

99
00:07:54,683 --> 00:07:56,768
The only reason I approached her
is 'cause she had several

100
00:07:56,852 --> 00:07:58,687
of the behavioral indicators
of a suicide bomber.

101
00:07:58,770 --> 00:07:59,938
Like what?

102
00:08:00,022 --> 00:08:01,190
You don't know them?

103
00:08:01,273 --> 00:08:03,442
Since 9/11,
every city cop in America knows them.

104
00:08:03,525 --> 00:08:06,028
How do you know them?
Were they trivia questions

105
00:08:06,111 --> 00:08:07,613
on the back of a creatine box?

106
00:08:07,696 --> 00:08:08,614
I was an MP.

107
00:08:09,615 --> 00:08:11,366
And I saw a nervous woman, sweating,

108
00:08:11,450 --> 00:08:13,619
fidgeting, mumbling, possibly praying,
looking straight ahead.

109
00:08:13,702 --> 00:08:15,829
So you don't have to see
the people you're about to kill.

110
00:08:15,913 --> 00:08:17,372
Wearing a heavy coat for the time
of year to hide explosives.

111
00:08:17,456 --> 00:08:20,250
Had a large bag.
She was checking all the boxes.

112
00:08:20,334 --> 00:08:24,004
Including the one
where she kills nobody except herself.

113
00:08:24,087 --> 00:08:25,380
You know what I think?

114
00:08:25,464 --> 00:08:26,673
Stupid things?

115
00:08:28,217 --> 00:08:29,676
I think you had something to do with it.

116
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:32,262
There were witnesses
on the train. Ask them.

117
00:08:32,346 --> 00:08:34,223
- They saw what happened.
- We did. They didn't.

118
00:08:34,306 --> 00:08:36,099
Some of them were asleep,
others weren't looking.

119
00:08:36,183 --> 00:08:37,976
Four witnesses and no one saw anything?

120
00:08:38,060 --> 00:08:40,020
-Three.
-There were four.

121
00:08:40,103 --> 00:08:43,440
A small Hispanic woman in her 40s,
Black man in his 30s,

122
00:08:43,523 --> 00:08:45,234
both tired, both coming off a night shift.

123
00:08:45,317 --> 00:08:46,735
Balkan immigrant, mid-20s.

124
00:08:46,818 --> 00:08:48,528
How the hell do you know
he was a Balkan immigrant?

125
00:08:48,612 --> 00:08:50,697
Coloring, height.

126
00:08:50,781 --> 00:08:52,950
People from that region
are taller on average.

127
00:08:53,033 --> 00:08:55,827
He was putting ketchup on his pizza,
which originated in Albania,

128
00:08:55,911 --> 00:08:58,997
and he was wearing a Colorado State
shirt that was spelled with all "O's."

129
00:08:59,081 --> 00:09:01,792
Irregular shirts are given to charities,
and he was wearing whatever

130
00:09:01,875 --> 00:09:04,211
hand-out fit. So, Balkan.

131
00:09:04,294 --> 00:09:05,879
Immigrant.

132
00:09:06,505 --> 00:09:09,424
Okay, Sherlock Has-No-Holmes,
that's three. You said four.

133
00:09:09,508 --> 00:09:11,426
Caucasian male. Mid-50s.

134
00:09:11,510 --> 00:09:13,804
Far end of the car. Tan pants. Golf shirt.

135
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:15,180
There was no one there like that.

136
00:09:15,806 --> 00:09:16,890
Then he took off in the confusion.

137
00:09:16,974 --> 00:09:19,810
Guns, dead bodies, lots of reasons to run.

138
00:09:19,893 --> 00:09:21,603
Maybe he told his wife
he was away on business,

139
00:09:21,687 --> 00:09:23,772
but he was taking the train
to see his girlfriend.

140
00:09:23,855 --> 00:09:26,316
I don't know. Who gives a shit?
But he was there.

141
00:09:26,984 --> 00:09:28,986
Did you kill Anna Merrick?
Was that your gun?

142
00:09:29,069 --> 00:09:31,113
What is this, good cop, dumb cop?

143
00:09:31,196 --> 00:09:33,156
She was killed with a .357 Magnum.

144
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:35,826
I don't have a drop of blood on me
and I'd have gun residue up to my wrist.

145
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:37,744
But when I got here,
you followed me into the bathroom

146
00:09:37,828 --> 00:09:39,329
and let me wash my hands.

147
00:09:39,413 --> 00:09:41,540
You wouldn't have done that
if you thought I shot this woman.

148
00:09:41,623 --> 00:09:43,458
You would have fingerprinted
and mirandized me.

149
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:46,586
You're stalling.

150
00:09:54,511 --> 00:09:57,347
You're right. We're holding onto you
because we got a call

151
00:09:57,431 --> 00:09:59,224
some other people want
to ask you some questions.

152
00:09:59,308 --> 00:10:00,851
Feds from D.C.

153
00:10:00,934 --> 00:10:02,144
How do you know that?

154
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:04,062
If it was FBI,
they'd be questioning me already

155
00:10:04,146 --> 00:10:05,814
'cause they have a branch office
here downtown.

156
00:10:07,274 --> 00:10:08,483
It's got to be folks up from D.C.

157
00:10:08,567 --> 00:10:12,404
CIA, DEA, DOD,
anyone else from the alphabet gang.

158
00:10:13,488 --> 00:10:15,657
Turns out our suicide worked
for the federal government.

159
00:10:15,741 --> 00:10:18,410
Somehow, that makes this all
a bit more complicated,

160
00:10:18,493 --> 00:10:21,079
so I'm asking you nicely,
if you could stay a while longer

161
00:10:21,163 --> 00:10:23,332
until they get here
and things are cleared up.

162
00:10:25,709 --> 00:10:27,336
I'll stay because
the Feds might know something

163
00:10:27,419 --> 00:10:29,046
about why she killed herself,
and I want to know.

164
00:10:29,129 --> 00:10:30,714
You said
you didn't know the victim.

165
00:10:30,797 --> 00:10:32,341
Why do you care?

166
00:10:32,424 --> 00:10:36,094
'Cause she was desperate
and needed help...

167
00:10:36,178 --> 00:10:37,304
and I didn't help her.

168
00:10:39,514 --> 00:10:42,142
Okay. So we wait a while.

169
00:10:42,225 --> 00:10:44,353
As for all this, you were a cop.

170
00:10:44,436 --> 00:10:45,729
You know we had to poke around,

171
00:10:45,812 --> 00:10:48,273
even though we know
you had nothing to do with what happened.

172
00:10:48,357 --> 00:10:52,277
Well, yeah, maybe not directly, but...

173
00:10:52,361 --> 00:10:54,738
That lady wasn't doing anything
until you ran up on her,

174
00:10:54,821 --> 00:10:57,783
got her all worked up enough
to off herself.

175
00:10:57,866 --> 00:11:00,243
Seen a few mass-transit suicides.

176
00:11:00,327 --> 00:11:01,912
People jump in front of trains.

177
00:11:01,995 --> 00:11:04,539
Not one has popped their top
on one of 'em.

178
00:11:04,623 --> 00:11:08,335
Sometimes people on the edge
get pushed over that edge.

179
00:11:08,418 --> 00:11:10,379
Maybe you were the pusher.

180
00:11:10,462 --> 00:11:13,298
And you'll stay here
because I'm telling you to stay.

181
00:11:14,341 --> 00:11:16,343
You really think
you can make me do anything?

182
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:31,525
Onions, peppers,

183
00:11:31,608 --> 00:11:33,819
-extra cheese.
-For what?

184
00:11:33,902 --> 00:11:35,487
My cheesesteak.

185
00:11:35,570 --> 00:11:36,780
It's gonna be a while.

186
00:11:36,863 --> 00:11:38,949
It's almost 5:00 a.m.

187
00:11:40,033 --> 00:11:41,034
I'm in Philly.

188
00:11:49,835 --> 00:11:51,128
It's not a bad breakfast.

189
00:11:51,211 --> 00:11:52,379
Told ya.

190
00:11:55,799 --> 00:11:56,925
What the hell is that?

191
00:11:57,008 --> 00:11:58,051
That's Gritty.

192
00:12:00,137 --> 00:12:01,263
Flyers mascot?

193
00:12:02,681 --> 00:12:04,433
-Not a hockey guy.
-Missing out.

194
00:12:04,516 --> 00:12:06,518
Perfect blend of speed,
skill and physicality.

195
00:12:06,601 --> 00:12:08,854
Two guys got beef, they battle it out.

196
00:12:08,937 --> 00:12:10,355
No politics, no bullshit.

197
00:12:10,439 --> 00:12:12,607
Well...

198
00:12:12,691 --> 00:12:13,900
some bullshit.

199
00:12:16,403 --> 00:12:17,821
Don't be shitty to my Gritty.

200
00:12:21,074 --> 00:12:22,325
So who'd you piss off?

201
00:12:22,409 --> 00:12:24,369
-What do you mean?
-Well, you're smart.

202
00:12:24,453 --> 00:12:26,079
Clearly smarter than your partner,

203
00:12:26,163 --> 00:12:29,124
but you're stuck on the night shift,
tasked with suicides.

204
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:31,001
That's incident reports, not police work.

205
00:12:32,419 --> 00:12:33,795
So, who'd you piss off?

206
00:12:35,422 --> 00:12:36,965
Mind your business.

207
00:12:43,555 --> 00:12:46,016
That's Anna's brother Jacob.

208
00:12:46,099 --> 00:12:47,601
Cop from Jersey.

209
00:12:48,435 --> 00:12:50,437
He's carrying himself
like someone still in shock.

210
00:12:51,188 --> 00:12:53,398
Shoulders down and rolled forward,
slouched.

211
00:12:53,482 --> 00:12:55,525
The primal instinct to protect yourself.

212
00:12:56,776 --> 00:12:57,903
It doesn't work.

213
00:13:03,325 --> 00:13:04,951
Feds will be here in a couple of minutes.

214
00:13:05,035 --> 00:13:06,369
Finish up.

215
00:13:28,850 --> 00:13:31,478
You don't seem very concerned
that we're here to question you.

216
00:13:31,561 --> 00:13:33,772
I was already questioned by Philly P.D.

217
00:13:33,855 --> 00:13:35,398
Did pretty well.

218
00:13:35,482 --> 00:13:37,484
Figured I'll only do better this time.

219
00:13:38,568 --> 00:13:39,986
So what agency you fellas with?

220
00:13:42,781 --> 00:13:44,074
What are your names?

221
00:13:49,704 --> 00:13:51,039
Okay.

222
00:13:51,122 --> 00:13:53,166
I'll call you Snap, Crackle and Pop.

223
00:13:53,875 --> 00:13:55,794
So what drags a bunch of B-Team boys
out to Philly?

224
00:13:55,877 --> 00:13:57,546
What makes you think we're the B-Team?

225
00:13:57,629 --> 00:14:00,173
Pulled out of bed to drive almost
three hours in the middle of the night

226
00:14:00,257 --> 00:14:02,384
to question somebody
you know wasn't involved in a shooting

227
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:03,885
'cause city cops already filled you in.

228
00:14:03,969 --> 00:14:06,513
You're here
so your bosses can put a little check

229
00:14:06,596 --> 00:14:10,600
in a little box that says you interviewed
the last person to talk to Anna Merrick.

230
00:14:10,684 --> 00:14:13,645
If you had the juice to say no,
you'd still be under your quilts.

231
00:14:15,814 --> 00:14:17,023
B-Team.

232
00:14:18,984 --> 00:14:20,443
Maybe C.

233
00:14:22,112 --> 00:14:23,989
So, I want to know
why the government's so interested

234
00:14:24,072 --> 00:14:25,865
in one of its employees killing herself.

235
00:14:25,949 --> 00:14:30,287
The way this works, see,
is you answer our questions.

236
00:14:30,370 --> 00:14:31,955
Why did you talk to Anna Merrick?

237
00:14:32,038 --> 00:14:33,582
I thought she was gonna blow up the train.

238
00:14:34,666 --> 00:14:37,085
You were military, Mr. Reacher,
highly decorated,

239
00:14:37,168 --> 00:14:39,963
but you left on not the best of terms.

240
00:14:40,964 --> 00:14:43,008
Any issues with the Army
or the government?

241
00:14:43,675 --> 00:14:45,051
Tons.

242
00:14:45,135 --> 00:14:46,511
Enough to do something about it?

243
00:14:47,470 --> 00:14:49,556
-Like what?
-Treason.

244
00:14:51,016 --> 00:14:52,559
Not really my style.

245
00:14:55,729 --> 00:14:57,397
Did you receive anything from Anna?

246
00:14:58,481 --> 00:14:59,691
Receive what?

247
00:14:59,774 --> 00:15:02,152
Maybe she gave you something,
and you ditched it,

248
00:15:02,235 --> 00:15:03,903
gonna go back for it later.

249
00:15:04,571 --> 00:15:07,907
Look, Crackle,
I was searched on the platform,

250
00:15:07,991 --> 00:15:09,909
and by now,
you've already picked the subway clean.

251
00:15:09,993 --> 00:15:12,329
Checked the platform,
looked under the seats,

252
00:15:12,412 --> 00:15:13,997
found nothing but gum and boogers.

253
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:16,374
If I ditched anything on the train,
you would have found it by now.

254
00:15:16,458 --> 00:15:19,461
What is it the government's so worried
she might've given me?

255
00:15:21,838 --> 00:15:24,299
- What are you looking for?
- Once again,

256
00:15:24,382 --> 00:15:26,092
we are here to ask the questions.

257
00:15:26,176 --> 00:15:27,677
You're here to answer them.

258
00:15:27,761 --> 00:15:29,262
Not anymore, Snap.

259
00:15:37,771 --> 00:15:39,731
Brought in for murder,
out with no charges.

260
00:15:39,814 --> 00:15:41,608
Better day than I had.

261
00:15:41,691 --> 00:15:44,152
Not my first time, won't be my last.

262
00:15:44,235 --> 00:15:45,945
Take care, Tamara.

263
00:15:47,197 --> 00:15:49,199
Yup.

264
00:16:07,842 --> 00:16:10,261
May I have a moment of your time?

265
00:16:11,262 --> 00:16:13,181
You just took a moment of my time.

266
00:16:13,264 --> 00:16:16,476
The woman who died in the subway,
did she give you anything?

267
00:16:16,559 --> 00:16:18,603
So far, nothing but hassle.

268
00:16:18,687 --> 00:16:20,355
Did you give it to the police?

269
00:16:20,438 --> 00:16:21,981
Give what to the police?

270
00:16:23,358 --> 00:16:25,235
The flash drive.

271
00:16:25,318 --> 00:16:27,654
I know messenger boys when I see 'em.

272
00:16:28,863 --> 00:16:31,783
So, who's your boss?

273
00:16:57,934 --> 00:17:01,271
♪ Well, down in Georgia,
they got a dance that's new ♪

274
00:17:01,354 --> 00:17:03,398
♪ Ain't nothin' to it,
'cause it's easy to do ♪

275
00:17:03,481 --> 00:17:04,899
Counter if it's just coffee.

276
00:17:04,983 --> 00:17:07,318
♪ Called "Shake That Thing" ♪

277
00:17:07,402 --> 00:17:10,655
♪ Oh, shake that thing ♪

278
00:17:10,739 --> 00:17:12,866
♪ I'm gettin' sick and tired...

279
00:17:12,949 --> 00:17:15,034
Jacob?

280
00:17:15,118 --> 00:17:16,536
Yeah.

281
00:17:18,913 --> 00:17:20,373
Do I know you?

282
00:17:20,457 --> 00:17:22,542
No, but I'm the last person
to talk to your sister.

283
00:17:22,625 --> 00:17:25,086
I'm a former cop. I can help.

284
00:17:25,170 --> 00:17:26,838
♪ Shake that thing...

285
00:17:26,921 --> 00:17:29,549
You decided?

286
