I only know what I saw.
A distraught woman.

294
00:17:52,739 --> 00:17:55,116
Two men outside jumped me
for some drive Anna was supposed to have.

295
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:56,826
You know anything about that?

296
00:17:56,910 --> 00:17:58,536
-Jumped you?
-Yeah.

297
00:17:58,620 --> 00:17:59,996
For a drive.

298
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:02,999
Like a... like a thumb drive?

299
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,834
-Apparently.
-No.

300
00:18:04,918 --> 00:18:07,921
No, I-I don't know anything about it. I...

301
00:18:08,004 --> 00:18:12,091
I just know that there is no way
that my sister killed herself.

302
00:18:12,175 --> 00:18:13,384
I saw her do it.

303
00:18:13,468 --> 00:18:15,470
I don't care what you saw.

304
00:18:16,596 --> 00:18:18,598
She was a happy person.

305
00:18:19,808 --> 00:18:21,810
She loved her job,

306
00:18:21,893 --> 00:18:24,854
she... loved my nephew Ben.

307
00:18:27,565 --> 00:18:29,317
Everything...

308
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:31,778
Everything was perfect.

309
00:18:31,861 --> 00:18:34,197
She didn't look
like everything was perfect.

310
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:35,990
She looked terrified.

311
00:18:36,866 --> 00:18:38,076
None of this makes any sense.

312
00:18:38,159 --> 00:18:40,703
You know why
she was wearing a winter coat in summer?

313
00:18:40,787 --> 00:18:43,122
No. I-I-I... I don't know.

314
00:18:43,206 --> 00:18:45,250
Maybe, um...

315
00:18:45,333 --> 00:18:46,751
Maybe she hid the gun in it.

316
00:18:46,835 --> 00:18:48,837
Gun was in the bag.

317
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,755
You know where she got the firearm?

318
00:18:50,839 --> 00:18:53,466
Before our dad died, he gave it to her.

319
00:18:53,550 --> 00:18:57,095
Single woman living alone.
You know, he worried.

320
00:18:57,178 --> 00:18:59,597
-Ben's father?
-That asshole's dead.

321
00:19:00,515 --> 00:19:03,643
The prick took off as soon
as the test showed two pink lines.

322
00:19:03,726 --> 00:19:07,146
A few months later,
he wrapped his car around a tree

323
00:19:07,230 --> 00:19:09,899
with half a bottle
of Johnnie Walker in him.

324
00:19:09,983 --> 00:19:11,776
You know, I helped raise my nephew.

325
00:19:13,862 --> 00:19:16,239
Paid for his braces
when things were tough.

326
00:19:17,824 --> 00:19:19,659
Bought him his first football.

327
00:19:20,827 --> 00:19:22,996
He's a linebacker at, uh, Temple.

328
00:19:24,414 --> 00:19:26,624
Full ride.

329
00:19:26,708 --> 00:19:29,127
♪ Morning, noon and night...

330
00:19:29,210 --> 00:19:31,504
I don't know how I'm gonna tell him.

331
00:19:31,588 --> 00:19:33,256
He doesn't know his mother's dead?

332
00:19:33,339 --> 00:19:34,966
No, I can't get ahold of him.

333
00:19:35,049 --> 00:19:36,843
That normal?

334
00:19:38,887 --> 00:19:42,098
I guess. I mean, he's...
he's a 20-year-old kid.

335
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:43,892
You know, he's got better things
to do than to jump

336
00:19:43,975 --> 00:19:46,477
when his uncle calls him
first thing in the morning.

337
00:19:46,561 --> 00:19:49,272
The Philly cops said Anna worked
for the federal government.

338
00:19:49,355 --> 00:19:50,565
Which part?

339
00:19:50,648 --> 00:19:52,984
Army Department, Human Resources,

340
00:19:53,067 --> 00:19:56,446
for some, uh, general or something.

341
00:19:56,529 --> 00:19:57,530
Must be a branch
of the Commanding General,

342
00:19:57,614 --> 00:20:01,534
U.S. Army, Human Resources Command.
Personnel department.

343
00:20:01,618 --> 00:20:03,119
Paperwork and records.

344
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:04,412
Nothing exciting.

345
00:20:04,495 --> 00:20:06,497
It was exciting to her.

346
00:20:06,581 --> 00:20:08,917
♪ Sit down, baby,
and have a little drink...

347
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:13,129
Getting out of the Jersey suburbs,
moving to D.C.

348
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:16,299
♪ Ain't no sense in you killing me...

349
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:18,718
I remember how proud she was when...

350
00:20:18,801 --> 00:20:22,680
♪ Morning, noon and night ♪

351
00:20:22,764 --> 00:20:24,140
♪ Love you, pretty baby ♪

352
00:20:24,223 --> 00:20:25,433
I'm sorry.

353
00:20:26,517 --> 00:20:28,061
♪ Morning, noon and night...

354
00:20:30,313 --> 00:20:31,814
We were both adopted.

355
00:20:34,651 --> 00:20:37,737
And we... we never fought.

356
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,697
Not once.

357
00:20:40,990 --> 00:20:43,201
I always thought I was so lucky.

358
00:20:45,078 --> 00:20:49,666
You know, out of all the kids in the world
that needed families,

359
00:20:49,749 --> 00:20:52,001
I got her to be my sister.

360
00:20:52,085 --> 00:20:53,336
They're back.

361
00:20:55,755 --> 00:20:56,965
What? Who?

362
00:20:57,048 --> 00:20:59,092
The guys who came after me
for your sister's drive.

363
00:20:59,175 --> 00:21:02,053
Recognize them?

364
00:21:02,136 --> 00:21:04,138
♪ Morning, noon and night ♪

365
00:21:04,222 --> 00:21:05,306
No.

366
00:21:06,391 --> 00:21:09,143
♪ Morning, noon and night ♪

367
00:21:09,227 --> 00:21:10,937
♪ Love you, pretty baby...

368
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:14,023
-50 bucks for your jump drive.
-Why?

369
00:21:14,107 --> 00:21:15,274
You always ask questions

370
00:21:15,358 --> 00:21:16,943
when someone offers you
five times the value of something?

371
00:21:17,026 --> 00:21:18,194
Okay, deal.

372
00:21:20,321 --> 00:21:21,614
What are you doing?

373
00:21:22,907 --> 00:21:24,325
Those guys were willing to come after me

374
00:21:24,409 --> 00:21:26,369
'cause they thought
Anna gave me something on the train.

375
00:21:26,452 --> 00:21:28,579
-I'm gonna find out why.
-Why do you care?

376
00:21:30,790 --> 00:21:32,291
Your sister's involved
in something big enough

377
00:21:32,375 --> 00:21:33,793
that the federal government's worried,

378
00:21:33,876 --> 00:21:36,462
and people are trying to work me over
on the street because of it.

379
00:21:36,546 --> 00:21:40,425
So big she saw no way out of it,
so she killed herself over it.

380
00:21:40,508 --> 00:21:42,051
I was the last person
that could've possibly helped her

381
00:21:42,135 --> 00:21:44,971
out of whatever situation
she was stuck in,

382
00:21:45,054 --> 00:21:46,931
and I didn't.

383
00:21:47,015 --> 00:21:49,392
-Then I'm coming.
-No. You're in uniform.

384
00:21:49,475 --> 00:21:51,102
You'll only complicate things.

385
00:21:51,185 --> 00:21:53,980
Stay here, keep trying
to get in touch with your nephew.

386
00:21:54,063 --> 00:21:55,565
He might know something.

387
00:21:55,648 --> 00:21:57,734
I'll be back in 90 minutes.

388
00:22:01,195 --> 00:22:02,739
Look what I got.

389
00:22:02,822 --> 00:22:04,782
Your boss wants it,
and I want some money and answers.

390
00:22:04,866 --> 00:22:06,993
You can set up a meeting,
or you can try and take it,

391
00:22:07,076 --> 00:22:08,536
and I can kick your asses again.

392
00:22:08,619 --> 00:22:11,164
Either option's fine with me.

393
00:22:24,969 --> 00:22:26,846
Thank you for meeting with me.

394
00:22:26,929 --> 00:22:28,556
It was my idea.

395
00:22:28,639 --> 00:22:32,393
Yeah, but after my cousins
crossed the line with you,

396
00:22:32,477 --> 00:22:34,312
I lost any hope we'd ever speak.

397
00:22:34,395 --> 00:22:38,024
So, thank you
for not holding their behavior against me.

398
00:22:38,107 --> 00:22:41,152
They could be very protective
of me and their aunt.

399
00:22:41,235 --> 00:22:42,904
My mother, Amisha Hoth.

400
00:22:45,448 --> 00:22:46,741
I'm Lila.

401
00:22:47,533 --> 00:22:49,410
Reacher.

402
00:22:49,494 --> 00:22:50,995
Your mother?

403
00:22:51,079 --> 00:22:54,624
She had me at 19, and it's been
just the two of us since then.

404
00:22:54,707 --> 00:22:56,959
Does she want the jump drive, too,
or just you?

405
00:23:00,505 --> 00:23:02,715
Walk with me, I'll explain everything.

406
00:23:10,348 --> 00:23:12,600
Did you know they call this place
the City of Brotherly Love?

407
00:23:14,185 --> 00:23:15,686
I like that.

408
00:23:15,770 --> 00:23:18,606
Their fans throw snowballs at Santa Claus.

409
00:23:20,358 --> 00:23:21,776
I don't understand.

410
00:23:22,735 --> 00:23:23,861
It doesn't matter.

411
00:23:25,113 --> 00:23:26,572
Look, I just want to know what's going on.

412
00:23:26,656 --> 00:23:28,699
♪ Bad machine, super cool, super mean...

413
00:23:28,783 --> 00:23:31,619
Oh. Best I start at the beginning.

414
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:35,581
In the '90s,
my mother met a U.S. soldier named John.

415
00:23:35,665 --> 00:23:37,917
He was in Delta Force.

416
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:40,962
She never learned his last name,
but they had an affair,

417
00:23:41,045 --> 00:23:43,172
and you're basically walking
with the result of that union.

418
00:23:44,882 --> 00:23:46,342
Okay.

419
00:23:48,177 --> 00:23:51,639
You're also walking
with a very sick person.

420
00:23:51,722 --> 00:23:53,724
I have leukemia.

421
00:23:55,351 --> 00:23:56,769
The bruises on your arm?

422
00:23:56,853 --> 00:23:59,355
My doctors say
I need a bone marrow transplant,

423
00:23:59,438 --> 00:24:01,274
but matches are hard to come by.

424
00:24:01,357 --> 00:24:03,985
And when you're mixed-race,
well, it's near impossible.

425
00:24:04,068 --> 00:24:06,362
What about your mother?

426
00:24:06,445 --> 00:24:09,073
Kidney disease, so, she can't donate.

427
00:24:10,116 --> 00:24:11,576
So your only hope is finding John?

428
00:24:11,659 --> 00:24:13,119
Yeah.

429
00:24:14,120 --> 00:24:17,373
I only know
he was stationed in Indonesia in '98.

430
00:24:17,456 --> 00:24:21,460
So I've contacted the Army,
veterans groups, military subreddits.

431
00:24:21,544 --> 00:24:23,171
Nothing worked.

432
00:24:24,422 --> 00:24:28,342
I eventually called the Pentagon, but just
got passed from department to department

433
00:24:28,426 --> 00:24:30,928
until I finally got in touch
with the most wonderful woman

434
00:24:31,012 --> 00:24:32,680
who worked in human resources.

435
00:24:32,763 --> 00:24:34,390
Anna Merrick.

436
00:24:34,473 --> 00:24:36,934
She was adopted,
so she understood the frustration

437
00:24:37,018 --> 00:24:39,520
of not knowing one's
full biological history.

438
00:24:39,604 --> 00:24:42,815
She worried if her son ever got sick,
she wouldn't know enough to help him.

439
00:24:43,900 --> 00:24:46,485
She promised to do all she could
to find my father, and she did.

440
00:24:47,570 --> 00:24:48,738
Someone important.

441
00:24:50,907 --> 00:24:52,825
You've looked on the drive?

442
00:24:52,909 --> 00:24:55,286
No, but the Feds wouldn't have been
asking about it

443
00:24:55,369 --> 00:24:57,455
unless it was someone important.

444
00:24:58,539 --> 00:25:00,625
Congressman John Sampson,

445
00:25:00,708 --> 00:25:02,543
Representative from North Carolina.

446
00:25:02,627 --> 00:25:04,128
You know him?

447
00:25:04,212 --> 00:25:07,089
Not really. Seen his name in the news.

448
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:10,551
The frontrunner
to be his party's presidential nominee.

449
00:25:10,635 --> 00:25:11,886
And his odds are good.

450
00:25:11,969 --> 00:25:15,389
Let me guess. He didn't want to talk.

451
00:25:15,473 --> 00:25:17,016
None of my messages were returned.

452
00:25:17,099 --> 00:25:19,268
So you're gonna blackmail him
with information

453
00:25:19,352 --> 00:25:21,187
Anna stole for you from the Pentagon.

454
00:25:22,605 --> 00:25:25,566
-That's what's on the drive.
-I know it's distasteful,

455
00:25:25,650 --> 00:25:27,652
but I'm 29 years old, Reacher.

456
00:25:27,735 --> 00:25:29,445
I don't want to die.

457
00:25:29,528 --> 00:25:32,740
Anna had documents proving Sampson
was in Indonesia when I was conceived.

458
00:25:32,823 --> 00:25:35,284
And along with my mother's testimony,

459
00:25:35,368 --> 00:25:37,870
well, I'm hoping
that creates enough public pressure

460
00:25:37,954 --> 00:25:39,705
to get him to take a DNA test.

461
00:25:39,789 --> 00:25:43,626
And if he's a match,
it would be political suicide

462
00:25:43,709 --> 00:25:45,962
for him not to donate his bone marrow
to his own child, right?

463
00:25:46,045 --> 00:25:49,090
Why did Anna want to meet in Philadelphia?

464
00:25:49,173 --> 00:25:51,092
She said D.C. was the most surveilled city
in the world,

465
00:25:51,175 --> 00:25:54,220
and technically, she was committing
espionage by giving me these files.

466
00:25:54,303 --> 00:25:57,265
I was supposed to meet her at my hotel,
but, of course, she never showed up.

467
00:25:57,348 --> 00:25:59,183
She killed herself.

468
00:26:00,518 --> 00:26:02,645
Yeah. I saw the news.

469
00:26:02,728 --> 00:26:04,230
Why?

470
00:26:05,564 --> 00:26:06,941
I wish I knew.

471
00:26:07,608 --> 00:26:10,236
But it kills me if what I asked of her
somehow led to it.

472
00:26:11,320 --> 00:26:14,657
Look, um, I don't have much...

473
00:26:16,033 --> 00:26:17,785
...but you can have all of it
for the drive.

474
00:26:19,870 --> 00:26:21,789
I'm sorry to get your hopes up.

475
00:26:21,872 --> 00:26:23,291
There's nothing on this.

476
00:26:36,971 --> 00:26:38,389
It's nothing but sketches.

477
00:26:38,597 --> 00:26:39,765
Check again.

478
00:26:40,099 --> 00:26:41,600
I got it from an art student.

479
00:26:41,684 --> 00:26:43,477
That's all there is.

480
00:26:44,478 --> 00:26:46,564
I didn't know your situation.

481
00:26:46,647 --> 00:26:48,357
I'm a former investigator.

482
00:26:48,441 --> 00:26:50,276
It's my nature to want information.

483
00:26:52,695 --> 00:26:54,989
Then the police must have the drive.

484
00:26:55,072 --> 00:26:56,282
Maybe.

485
00:26:56,365 --> 00:26:58,034
But if they did,
the Feds wouldn't have been asking

486
00:26:58,117 --> 00:26:59,368
if Anna gave it to me this morning.

487
00:27:00,953 --> 00:27:02,455
Yeah, I-I understand.

488
00:27:02,538 --> 00:27:06,334
I'm-I'm staying at The Carter Hotel
on 10th Street

489
00:27:06,417 --> 00:27:08,836
until Anna's funeral is arranged.

490
00:27:08,919 --> 00:27:11,547
I mean, she was a friend
who died helping me.

491
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:13,591
It's the least I could do.

492
00:27:13,674 --> 00:27:17,011
Here's my cell and my room number.

493
00:27:17,094 --> 00:27:19,096
Uh, thumb drive...

494
00:27:22,767 --> 00:27:26,395
If you find anything, please.

495
00:27:26,479 --> 00:27:28,606
What makes you think I'll keep looking?

496
00:27:29,940 --> 00:27:32,526
Like you said,
you're a former investigator.

497
00:27:32,610 --> 00:27:35,071
It's in your nature to want information.

498
00:27:38,699 --> 00:27:39,867
Good luck, Lila.

499
00:27:48,667 --> 00:27:50,211
♪ Well, I must have been stoned ♪

500
00:27:51,587 --> 00:27:53,255
♪ When this whole thing started ♪

501
00:27:58,052 --> 00:28:02,890
♪ 'Cause I just can't seem
to think straight anymore...

502
00:28:02,973 --> 00:28:04,517
I gave her $40.

503
00:28:04,600 --> 00:28:07,645
It's been over an hour.
She-she was getting pissed.

504
00:28:07,728 --> 00:28:09,397
How'd your nephew take the news?

505
00:28:09,480 --> 00:28:11,190
I didn't track him down yet.

506
00:28:12,191 --> 00:28:14,068
What about you? What about...
did you find anything?

507
00:28:14,151 --> 00:28:17,321
Yeah. Seems your sister
may have stolen some confidential

508
00:28:17,405 --> 00:28:19,573
albeit pretty benign data
about Congressman John Sampson

509
00:28:19,657 --> 00:28:21,575
to help a woman prove he was her father.

510
00:28:22,493 --> 00:28:23,577
What else?

511
00:28:24,245 --> 00:28:25,454
That's it.

512
00:28:27,832 --> 00:28:29,166
John Sampson?

513
00:28:29,250 --> 00:28:30,709
John Sampson.

514
00:28:32,461 --> 00:28:34,171
Where you going?

515
00:28:35,339 --> 00:28:37,800
I'm gonna find out all I can
about John Sampson.

516
00:28:38,884 --> 00:28:42,721
Not my business, but the federal
government's looking into this.

517
00:28:42,805 --> 00:28:45,599
What do you think a solo cop
from a small town in Jersey's gonna do?

518
00:28:45,683 --> 00:28:47,435
I have no idea.

519
00:28:48,602 --> 00:28:52,231
But my sister died because she was trying
to help somebody find their father.

520
00:28:53,232 --> 00:28:55,651
That is exactly who Anna was.

521
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:59,238
She never let anyone down,
and I'm not gonna let her down.

522
00:29:03,117 --> 00:29:04,785
Okay.

523
00:29:04,869 --> 00:29:06,495
Let's go.

524
00:29:07,746 --> 00:29:08,914
You're coming?

525
00:29:12,042 --> 00:29:14,753
I'm good at not letting people
get away with things.

526
00:29:26,807 --> 00:29:28,476
Hey! What are you doing?

527
00:29:28,559 --> 00:29:30,186
Taking our files.

528
00:29:30,978 --> 00:29:32,021
Your files are in D.C.

529
00:29:32,104 --> 00:29:34,023
-My desk is right here.
-Easy, killer.

530
00:29:34,106 --> 00:29:36,025
They're taking over
the Anna Merrick suicide.

531
00:29:36,108 --> 00:29:38,903
What's there to take over?
The case ended when the woman died.

532
00:29:38,986 --> 00:29:40,821
The files, please, Detective.

533
00:29:40,905 --> 00:29:42,740
The captain signed off on it.

534
00:29:53,959 --> 00:29:56,504
- Assholes.
- Why the hell do you care?

535
00:29:57,588 --> 00:30:00,090
Machine fucked you sideways,
you still didn't learn?

536
00:30:00,174 --> 00:30:03,636
Punch in, punch out,
hope the phone doesn't ring in between.

537
00:30:03,719 --> 00:30:05,930
It's about the income, not the outcome.

538
00:30:06,013 --> 00:30:07,765
I know.

539
00:30:07,848 --> 00:30:09,266
But still.

540
00:30:10,267 --> 00:30:12,269
Touching my shit.

541
00:30:16,524 --> 00:30:17,775
No scandals,

542
00:30:17,858 --> 00:30:19,735
no black marks.

543
00:30:19,818 --> 00:30:22,363
No politician's this clean.

544
00:30:24,990 --> 00:30:27,243
Why are you printing them?

545
00:30:27,326 --> 00:30:29,954
It's information on the guy.

546
00:30:30,037 --> 00:30:32,831
It's superficial horseshit.

547
00:30:32,915 --> 00:30:35,584
It... it's background.

548
00:30:35,668 --> 00:30:37,836
I need his military data.

549
00:30:37,920 --> 00:30:40,798
Delta Force records would be confidential,
but there could be government documents

550
00:30:40,881 --> 00:30:44,468
that speak generally to overseas missions
Sampson might have been involved in.

551
00:30:44,552 --> 00:30:46,971
Could shed some light on who this guy is.

552
00:30:48,639 --> 00:30:49,765
Excuse me.

553
00:30:50,599 --> 00:30:52,101
Where are your military archives?

554
00:30:52,184 --> 00:30:54,812
Oh, like old stuff?
Old stuff's in the basement.

555
00:30:56,564 --> 00:30:59,525
Guess I'm headed to the basement
to look for "old stuff."

556
00:32:19,021 --> 00:32:20,856
Give me the drive.

557
00:32:22,566 --> 00:32:23,734
No.

558
00:34:01,373 --> 00:34:02,750
We need to go.

559
00:34:02,833 --> 00:34:04,460
Lila Hoth's in trouble.

560
00:34:11,675 --> 00:34:14,052
A coal bin?

561
00:34:14,136 --> 00:34:16,972
-I'm a cop! You can't do shit like that.
-Shut up.

562
00:34:17,055 --> 00:34:18,557
Please leave
a message after the tone.

563
00:34:18,640 --> 00:34:20,476
Lila, it's Reacher.

564
00:34:20,559 --> 00:34:22,311
Someone just took a run at me,
they might be coming after you.

565
00:34:22,394 --> 00:34:24,021
Get out of your hotel.

566
00:34:26,106 --> 00:34:28,442
-How much further?
-A couple minutes.

567
00:34:29,860 --> 00:34:31,487
I'm calling again.

568
00:35:06,355 --> 00:35:08,232
-They're at the top floors.
-Room 506.

569
00:35:08,315 --> 00:35:09,942
Take the west stairs.

570
00:35:41,223 --> 00:35:42,224
Lila!

571
00:35:43,267 --> 00:35:44,434
Stay there!

572
00:36:55,005 --> 00:36:56,131
Oh, shit.

573
00:36:59,509 --> 00:37:00,594
What?

574
00:37:06,934 --> 00:37:07,935
Get back inside.

575
00:37:17,486 --> 00:37:18,862
You okay?

576
00:37:18,946 --> 00:37:20,280
I think so.

577
00:37:24,952 --> 00:37:26,620
I think my nose is broken.

578
00:37:27,287 --> 00:37:28,622
Cops will be here any minute.

579
00:37:28,705 --> 00:37:30,666
-Let's move.
-But we're the good guys.

580
00:37:30,749 --> 00:37:32,542
You want to answer questions
about why you're here?

581
00:37:32,626 --> 00:37:35,087
Blackmailing's a crime
no matter how good the reason.

582
00:37:37,422 --> 00:37:38,799
-Where's your family?
-Getting food.

583
00:37:38,882 --> 00:37:40,842
I'll call and tell them
not to come back here.

584
00:37:40,926 --> 00:37:44,054
Do it after you get dressed.
We got to move, now.

585
00:37:51,395 --> 00:37:53,188
Keep your heads down.

586
00:37:53,271 --> 00:37:55,273
-Lose the washcloth.
-It's bleeding.

587
00:37:58,360 --> 00:37:59,778
Menus.

588
00:38:07,411 --> 00:38:08,912
There'll be more.

589
00:38:08,996 --> 00:38:10,664
Hotel staff will be able to describe you.

590
00:38:10,747 --> 00:38:13,000
Go buy new clothes.
Grays, dark blues, muted colors.

591
00:38:13,083 --> 00:38:14,209
Why?

592
00:38:14,292 --> 00:38:15,961
'Cause you don't want to stand out.

593
00:38:16,044 --> 00:38:18,380
And a woman like you
stands out enough as it is.

594
00:38:18,463 --> 00:38:20,340
Go see your mom.

595
00:38:20,424 --> 00:38:22,384
Get a shit-box, all-cash motel.

596
00:38:22,467 --> 00:38:24,720
Won't be nice, but it'll be safe.

597
00:38:24,803 --> 00:38:26,054
Where are you going?

598
00:38:26,138 --> 00:38:27,389
I got to go see a cop.

599
00:38:37,441 --> 00:38:39,901
No, no, that's fine. It is.
Okay, all right.

600
00:38:39,985 --> 00:38:41,862
When he gets back,
you got to have him call me.

601
00:38:41,945 --> 00:38:44,448
This is really, really important, okay?

602
00:38:45,741 --> 00:38:46,783
Thank you.

603
00:38:48,702 --> 00:38:50,662
One of Ben's frat brothers

604
00:38:50,746 --> 00:38:53,373
says a day and a half ago,
he left a bar with some gorgeous woman

605
00:38:53,457 --> 00:38:55,167
and he hasn't returned to campus yet.

606
00:38:56,835 --> 00:38:58,795
I'm gonna let him have his fun.

607
00:38:58,879 --> 00:39:00,922
His whole world's about
to get rocked soon when I talk to him.

608
00:39:01,006 --> 00:39:03,300
-Or when he sees it on the news.
-There she is.

609
00:39:04,426 --> 00:39:06,511
What the fuck now?

610
00:39:06,595 --> 00:39:09,473
-You were waiting for me?
-Need to ask you something.

611
00:39:10,557 --> 00:39:12,100
Detective Tamara Green.

612
00:39:12,184 --> 00:39:13,435
Sorry about your sister.

613
00:39:13,518 --> 00:39:15,437
Look, I just punched out.

614
00:39:15,520 --> 00:39:17,856
You should've come in when I was still
getting paid to deal with the public.

615
00:39:17,939 --> 00:39:19,900
Wouldn't have. Docherty doesn't like me.

616
00:39:19,983 --> 00:39:21,568
Would've talked you out
of doing me a favor.

617
00:39:21,651 --> 00:39:24,404
That old man couldn't talk me out of shit.

618
00:39:24,488 --> 00:39:25,822
What do you want?

619
00:39:25,906 --> 00:39:27,699
Has a jump drive turned up
since I left this morning?

620
00:39:27,783 --> 00:39:29,159
Now you sound like the Feds.

621
00:39:30,077 --> 00:39:31,161
They were looking for it, too.

622
00:39:31,244 --> 00:39:32,370
First thing they asked for.

623
00:39:32,454 --> 00:39:34,289
I'm-a tell you the same thing I told them.

624
00:39:34,372 --> 00:39:37,084
I inventoried all the evidence and
personal effects before they got there,

625
00:39:37,167 --> 00:39:38,502
and there was no flash drive.

626
00:39:41,630 --> 00:39:42,964
Why? What's on it?

627
00:39:43,048 --> 00:39:44,174
Don't know.

628
00:39:44,257 --> 00:39:46,176
But people think Anna Merrick gave me one.

629
00:39:46,259 --> 00:39:47,636
Two people tried to kill me over it.

630
00:39:47,719 --> 00:39:48,887
Since I saw you this morning?

631
00:39:48,970 --> 00:39:50,263
Busy day.

632
00:39:50,347 --> 00:39:52,057
One came at me at a library,
one at a hotel.

633
00:39:52,140 --> 00:39:54,101
What happened to those people?

634
00:39:55,685 --> 00:39:56,812
They got away.

635
00:39:56,895 --> 00:39:58,897
Is there any chance
that the Feds maybe said

636
00:39:58,980 --> 00:40:00,524
-anything about why they--
-Look,

637
00:40:00,607 --> 00:40:02,943
all I know is a woman killed herself
on one of my subways.

638
00:40:03,026 --> 00:40:05,487
She was important enough that the Feds
officially took over the matter.

639
00:40:05,570 --> 00:40:08,031
Now you say people coming after you
for some jump drive?

640
00:40:08,115 --> 00:40:10,158
And I think you may have done
some bad shit to them.

641
00:40:10,242 --> 00:40:12,744
Like I said, they got away.

642
00:40:12,828 --> 00:40:14,663
Your knuckle's all jacked up,
your face is bruised

643
00:40:14,746 --> 00:40:17,457
and you got dry blood behind your ear.

644
00:40:17,541 --> 00:40:19,251
Blood's not mine.

645
00:40:20,961 --> 00:40:23,839
Know what? Not my monkeys, not my circus.

646
00:40:23,922 --> 00:40:26,508
I deal with OD'ing junkies
and Wawa smash-and-grabs.

647
00:40:26,591 --> 00:40:29,261
You want to run around
like a cowboy, go ahead.

648
00:40:29,344 --> 00:40:31,471
I'm-a run out five years
and collect my pension.

649
00:40:31,555 --> 00:40:33,431
I'm coming off a double night.

650
00:40:33,515 --> 00:40:36,852
I'm gonna head home,
watch SportsCenter and hit the sack.

651
00:40:36,935 --> 00:40:39,688
You need extra help? You got Barney Fife.

652
00:40:39,771 --> 00:40:41,565
Once again, sorry for your loss.

653
00:40:43,942 --> 00:40:45,485
Now what?

654
00:40:45,569 --> 00:40:47,362
We talk to Sampson.

655
00:40:47,445 --> 00:40:49,698
-You're driving.
-To D.C.?

656
00:40:49,781 --> 00:40:52,450
-Just a day or two.
-No, no, I can't take the cruiser.

657
00:40:52,534 --> 00:40:54,286
I'll get in trouble.

658
00:40:54,369 --> 00:40:56,079
I got to bring it back to Jersey.

659
00:40:56,163 --> 00:41:00,375
There's a 6:00 p.m. train to D.C.
every night from Penn Station.

660
00:41:00,458 --> 00:41:01,835
I'll meet you there.

661
00:41:03,170 --> 00:41:04,629
Okay.

662
00:41:06,631 --> 00:41:07,883
Okay.

663
00:41:08,884 --> 00:41:10,010
Okay.

664
00:41:22,981 --> 00:41:24,524
We'd like to talk to you.

665
00:41:24,608 --> 00:41:27,986
Strangers in suits who want to talk
in the middle of the day?

666
00:41:28,069 --> 00:41:29,821
You guys handing out The Watchtower?

667
00:41:31,239 --> 00:41:32,407
Tranq gun?

668
00:41:32,490 --> 00:41:34,409
Enough to take down a gorilla.

669
00:41:34,492 --> 00:41:36,369
We'll see.

670
00:41:36,453 --> 00:41:38,538
Take him.

671
00:41:43,293 --> 00:41:45,587
No point in trying to fight, Mr. Reacher.

672
00:41:45,670 --> 00:41:46,838
The drug is al--

673
00:41:52,135 --> 00:41:53,303
Come on.

